# wie_validate --keys: LGT 3cc7a9b4cb15 — notices → title → menu → new game → the intro's castle dialogue,
# the heaviest scene a native run reaches without a save (docs/report/0557 §3 · 0559 §4).
# Grammar: `--keys` help / `parse_keys` in wie_cli/src/bin/wie_validate.rs. Key names only — no game bytes.
#
# The path must not depend on WHEN the title's «press any key» becomes ready — on a busy host it is not
# ready by the 8th OK, and a script that counts on that OK ends one key short, on the character screen
# (load1 59, docs/report/0575 §2). So: two LEFTs after the wait. Whichever key opens the menu, the rest
# are no-ops on it, and the menu is left on its first row. From there four OKs: first row → first (empty)
# slot → «start a new game?» yes → the offered character.
#
# After the last OK the intro narrates by itself and then stops on the first dialogue page of the castle
# scene, which waits for a key. No key is sent after that, so the page stays up: with `--boot-secs 12` it
# is there by process time ~100 s and any later window profiles it. Look at the t100+ shots before
# reading a profile — a profile of the wrong screen is still a profile.
#
#   bash scripts/arm-interp-profile.sh <wie_validate> <game> docs/keys/lgt-3cc7a9b4cb15-intro-castle.keys 110 <out>
OK:1 OK:1 OK:1 OK:1 OK:3 OK:4 OK:3 OK:4 WAIT:14 LEFT:2 LEFT:2 OK:3 OK:4 OK:4 OK:9
WAIT:30 WAIT:30 WAIT:30 WAIT:30
